#!/bin/sh
# Send a netmode message to Telegram. Settings in /etc/config/netmode: telegram (on/off), telegram_token
# (from @BotFather), telegram_chat (user, group or channel id). Buttons are answered by netmode-bot.
#   notify [-k keyboard_json] "text"   send if notifications are on and not muted (/mute in the bot)
#   notify -t ["text"]                 test: send even if they are off and print the result
. /lib/functions.sh
config_load netmode
config_get_bool ON main telegram 0
config_get TOKEN main telegram_token ""
config_get CHAT main telegram_chat ""

test=0; kb=""
while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
	case "$1" in
		-t) test=1; shift ;;
		-k) kb=$2; shift 2 ;;
		*) break ;;
	esac
done
text=${1:-"✅ netmode on $(uci -q get system.@system[0].hostname): Telegram notifications work."}
if [ $test = 0 ]; then
	[ "$ON" = 1 ] || exit 0
	mu=$(cat /var/run/netmode/mute_until 2>/dev/null)
	[ -n "$mu" ] && [ "$mu" -gt "$(date +%s)" ] && exit 0
fi
if [ -z "$TOKEN" ] || [ -z "$CHAT" ]; then
	echo "set the bot token and the chat id first"; exit 1
fi

if [ -n "$kb" ]; then set -- --data-urlencode "reply_markup=$kb"; else set --; fi
reply=$(curl -sS -m 15 -X POST "https://api.telegram.org/bot$TOKEN/sendMessage" \
	-d "chat_id=$CHAT" -d "disable_web_page_preview=true" --data-urlencode "text=$text" "$@" 2>&1)
if echo "$reply" | grep -q '"ok":true'; then
	[ $test = 1 ] && echo "sent"
	exit 0
fi
err=$(echo "$reply" | jsonfilter -e '@.description' 2>/dev/null); err=${err:-$reply}
logger -t netmode "telegram: not sent ($err)"
[ $test = 1 ] && echo "not sent: $err"
exit 1
